=== A5 Nether emissive / block-light probe ===
Astra applies ONE multiplier to every species (nether_light.csh:34); the
reference gives each kind its own (lib/vx/blocklightColor.glsl).

--- Part 1: voxel emission, Astra before -> after vs reference ---
  kind                                     Astra x1.5               Astra x3.5               reference
  3 orange (torch, magma, campfire...)     (1.50, 0.45, 0.068)   (3.50, 1.05, 0.158)   (3.50, 1.75, 0.53)
  11 lava                                  (1.50, 0.27, 0.038)   (3.50, 0.63, 0.088)   (5.00, 0.90, 0.10)
  4 yellow (glowstone, redstone lamp)      (1.50, 0.99, 0.330)   (3.50, 2.31, 0.770)   (5.50, 3.30, 1.65)
  10 soul fire                             (0.08, 0.93, 1.500)   (0.19, 2.17, 3.500)   (0.35, 2.10, 3.50)

  ratio to reference on the dominant channel, before -> after:
    3 orange (torch, magma, campfire...)     0.43 -> 1.00
    11 lava                                  0.30 -> 0.70
    4 yellow (glowstone, redstone lamp)      0.27 -> 0.64
    10 soul fire                             0.43 -> 1.00

  x3.5 is the reference multiplier for the torch / soul / candle family, the
  Nether's most common emitters; the single-multiplier design cannot match the
  *2.0 magma and *5.5 glowstone ends at the same time. Before the change every
  family sat at 26-43% of the reference; after it the torch family matches and
  lava reaches 70%.

--- Part 2: block light + held light composition ---
  Astra nether_block_lighting():  I = pow(block,2.75)*B + pow(held,2.75)
  reference mainLighting.glsl:765: block = sqrt(block^2 + held^2)
    block=0.50 held=0.00 | straight sum 0.1487 -> sqrt-sum 0.1487 (x1.000) | reference sqrt-sum
    block=1.00 held=0.00 | straight sum 1.0000 -> sqrt-sum 1.0000 (x1.000) | reference sqrt-sum
    block=0.50 held=0.50 | straight sum 0.2973 -> sqrt-sum 0.2102 (x0.707) | reference sqrt-sum
    block=1.00 held=1.00 | straight sum 1.0000 -> sqrt-sum 1.0000 (x1.000) | reference sqrt-sum
    block=0.80 held=0.30 | straight sum 0.5779 -> sqrt-sum 0.5426 (x0.939) | reference sqrt-sum

  with no hand light the two forms agree exactly (held=0 -> sqrt(b^2) = b), so
  the change only affects frames where a light source is held: it removes the
  early saturation to 1.0 and keeps colour separation between the two sources.
  BLOCKLIGHT_COLOR (4.4, 2.9, 1.7) is unchanged.

--- Part 3: the :142-152 lighting block, Astra vs reference, item by item ---
  sceneLighting base     identical
      reference: (netherColor + 0.5*lavaLightColor)*(0.9+0.45*vs)
      Astra    : (netherCol + 0.5*NETHER_LAVA_LIGHT_COLOR)*(0.9+0.45*VS)
  lava direction term    identical
      reference: lavaLightColor * pow2(|NdotN|*0.5 + max0(-NdotU))*(0.7+0.35*vs)
      Astra    : NETHER_LAVA_LIGHT_COLOR * (lavaDir*lavaDir) * (0.7 + 0.35*VS)
  min-light base         identical
      reference: 0.005625 + vsBrightness * 0.043
      Astra    : 0.005625 + NETHER_VS_BRIGHTNESS * 0.043
  min-light tint         identical
      reference: vec3(0.45, 0.475, 0.6)
      Astra    : NETHER_FLOOR_TINT
  min-light block fade   identical
      reference: * (1.0 - lightmapYM)
      Astra    : * (1.0 - blockLight)
  night-vision add       identical
      reference: + nightVision * vec3(0.5, 0.5, 0.75)
      Astra    : + params.nightVision * NETHER_NIGHT_VISION_TINT_REF

  => the :142-152 block needs no change: every factor already matches the
     reference source line by line. The measured gap was in nether_light.csh.
